: mk - build Archaic on Idris. First sh mkinc once, then sh mk.
: Each c also tries to link and prints undefined names. That is fine,
: the link at the end, sh lka, is the real one.
: main.c has more than 32 KB of code. as.68k reaches a function in the
: same file with a 16-bit offset, so main.c goes through the passes of c
: by hand, with as.68k -z: all calls get a 32-bit address.
: as.68k then says 16-bit value exceeded and word pc range for branches
: back to a label past 32 KB. These messages are false: the code is right.
/etc/bin/pp -o main.i -x -i "|/lib/hdrs/|/lib/hdrs/sys/" +std /lib/hdrs/id68kn.h main.c
/odd/p1 -o main.1 -m -r6 -alu -rf main.rf +std main.i
/odd/p2.68k -o main.s -x4 -rf main.rf main.1
/etc/bin/as.68k -o main.o -10 -x -z main.s
rm main.i main.1 main.rf main.s
